{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1199025-brainstorming-other-prey","id":1199025,"title":"Brainstorming Other \"Prey\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-24T06:47:26-07:00","id":1199025,"title":"Brainstorming Other \"Prey\"","content":"So while thinking about my &quot;homebrew Firstborn&quot; thread, I've started thinking about more forms of an &quot;exotic prey&quot; which the Uratha may stumble upon during their hunt. Now, I'm not saying that the existing prey types are bad or limited or anything (that is, the &quot;tribal five&quot; + Idigam), but as you can't have too many antagonists, I thought that developing new things for the Forsaken to hunt could always be a good thing :P. Anyway, here is what I've had in mind-<br /> <br /> - the Drowned: when Sundered World has just came out, and people has started to talk about all the new Pangaeans, I remember how Sea was described as &quot;one of the most terrifying&quot; of the ancient horrors. Now, I don't remember if Sea showed up in the book or that it was something Chris Allen just mentioned in the forums, but the concepts of undersea horrors is something which is always fun to explore, especially considering that it is already touched in the Brineborn's writeup, the Drowned of UK or that sea monster from Predators. As such, trying to tie it all together to a single paradigm of the &quot;spawn of the Drowning Queen&quot; could be nice thing to do. Besides, it may give you an excuse to do a marine campaign and scream &quot;release the KRAKEN&quot; in the middle of the game :P<br /> <br /> - the Underfolk: but horrors don't have to come from the ocean's depths- they could also rise right beneath our feet. From the morlocks from the Time Machine to the Underdark of D&amp;D )FR especially), the idea of ancient and forgotten civilization which exist bellow earth and that leave their hideouts in order to prey upon the world above could give nice new form of prey to deal with. To that we could add the concept of forbidden spirits and banished gods which were &quot;trapped by Gaea's warm embrace&quot; (partially stolen from Exalted), and you'll have a decent base material to work with in order to design the legions of terror which hide beneath the surface.<br /> <br /> - Stymphalians: the truth is, that the concept for sea and underground specific &quot;prey&quot; came to me when I read about one of the lesser known Firstborn, called the Sky Hunter, which made me think about sky specific monsters. Now, while I've eventually gave up on the idea for the tribe, I do think it may have some potential to explore- and considering that as a child I made my &quot;greek mythology project&quot; around the Stymphalian Birds, it looks to me like a nice place to start. The concept of avian monstrosities could also be explored in relation to the Distant Ones, the Bird Pangaean, the Eye from Five Pounds of Meat, the Ugallu and similar other mentions of winged horrors which have already mentioned in the setting.<br /> <br /> - Void Spirits: we all know they exist, and we all want more about them. The Void Leviathans which comes from beyond the world and which Luna guards against are terrible horrors by their own right, and I don't I even need to explain why having those alien terrors from outer space is something you want (and the Forsaken really don't want) to see.<br /> <br /> - Leshy: so we have horrors of the sea, the sky, bellow the ground and from the heaven above- that leaves the horrors of the earth itself, doesn't it? Being presented in the Field of Dogs' Hunting Ground, I think that the Leshy, as the monsters of the forest, have some interesting potential to develop for that niche. Now, I know that the book suggest that they may be a some form of Claimed- but it is done from the Uratha's point of view- and the Forsaken are quick to condemn any new being they don't understand as &quot;Claimed&quot;. The book itself presents them as somewhat a mystery, and mysteries are to be explored. After all, the Colony is usually seen as the &quot;Cat Host&quot;. It is not out of the picture that the Leshy are a spiritual breed on their own right.<br /> <br /> So- what do you think about those? Feel free to suggest other new concepts of prey of your own :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T07:00:26-07:00","id":1199031,"title":"","content":"The Astral is always ready for mining ideas from (sometimes literally), even before getting into crossover with Beast or Mage. Especially with Cahalith dreaming their way into the Dreaming Earth / Anima Mundi / Mother\u2019s Land.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T07:31:29-07:00","id":1199048,"title":"","content":"I was interested in Foresaken repelling Alien Invaders from Beyond the Stars, but that could fall into the Sky and Void category?<br /> <br /> But I totally love the idea of Foresaken charged with slaying the Vanguards or Sentries of a conquering horde.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}